    <marc:datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">This two-part volume addresses the specific area of interdisciplinary connections within special education research.  Special education has transformed as a result of legislation, new trends and current research investigations.  Currently, there is no comprehensive resource that effectively covers these advances. Continuing the approach of part a, part b allows readers to follow interdisciplinary connections within special education as it relates to the roles of audiologists, surgeons, vision specialists and school nurses</marc:subfield>
